    "text": "Moment of inertia of a cylinder of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> and radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> about an axis passing through its centre and perpendicular to the axis of the cylinder is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> If such a cylinder is to be made for a given mass of a material, the ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></math> for it to have minimum possible <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> is:"
